<Project>
  <!--
    arb-egr: emits an XML doc file for every project so malformed XML on load-bearing
    comments (CS1570/CS1571/CS1572/CS1580/CS1584/CS1587/CS1589/CS1590/CS1592, etc.) becomes a
    real build warning and fails the 0-warnings gate in CLAUDE.md section 5, instead of being
    silently generated-but-unchecked as it was before this file existed.

    CS1591 and CS1573 are suppressed by choice, not by omission: a missing summary or an
    incomplete <param> list is "missing documentation", the same class CS1591 already covers,
    not malformed XML, so the gate does not need to see it.

    CS1574 and CS0419 (an unresolved or ambiguous <see>/<paramref> cref) are NOT suppressed: they
    were fixed wholesale under arb-ul4 and are real warnings that fail the build, which is what
    keeps a cref honest. A cref rots silently when the symbol it names is renamed, made private, or
    moved into a project this one may not reference (Core may not reference Api or Data, per
    CoreIsolationTests) — the comment then points at nothing while still reading as a live link.
    When a referent is genuinely unreachable, or is a concept, a JSON field, a setting-key string or
    a route rather than a symbol, write it as plain <c>Name</c> code text. Never add a project
    reference, never widen a member's accessibility, and never delete the doc comment, merely to
    make a cref resolve.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CS1573</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
